'' A byref function must set its result somewhere (fbc 316; one branch or a return is
'' enough); a byref result must be assigned something with an address (24 for a literal
'' or an address-of, 3 for an expression; a string literal into 'byref as zstring' is
'' fine); a qualified declare or definition into a TYPE that never declared the name is
'' 158, and so is a second declare of a declared member; the alias on a definition must
'' match its declaration's (311). Matches fbc on lines 33, 35, 38, 41, 43, 44 and 46;
'' fbc's 316 on 36 and 39 is a cascade from the refused assignment and is not repeated;
'' the never-set report sits on the 'function' line (32) where fbc uses 'end function'.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/byref-result-and-owner.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' GOLDEN: expected/byref-result-and-owner.out
